---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../content/site';
import { url } from '../utils/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Support — ${site.name}`}
  description={`Get help with ${site.name}. Supported platforms, audio formats, Apple Music requirements, and contact information.`}
>
  <article class="section container prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>

    <h2>How to Get Help</h2>
    <p>
      <!-- TODO: Replace with real support email or support form URL -->
      For support, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
      We aim to respond within a few business days.
    </p>

    <h2>Supported Platforms</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} requires iPhone or iPad running iOS 26 or later.
      The app is a universal binary optimized for both devices.
    </p>

    <h2>Supported Audio Formats</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>M4A (AAC)</li>
      <li>MP3</li>
      <li>WAV</li>
      <li>AIFF</li>
      <li>CAF</li>
      <li>M4R</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Import audio files from the Files app, or use drag and drop on iPad.
    </p>

    <h2>Apple Music Requirements</h2>
    <p>
      Apple Music features in {site.name} require an active Apple Music subscription and an active internet
      connection. Local audio playback works entirely offline and does not require Apple Music.
    </p>

    <h2>Common Questions</h2>

    <h3>The app won't play audio</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Make sure your device is not in Silent Mode.</li>
      <li>Check that the volume is turned up and not muted in the mixer.</li>
      <li>Verify the audio file is in a supported format.</li>
      <li>Try restarting the app.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Apple Music isn't playing or connecting</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Ensure you have an active Apple Music subscription.</li>
      <li>Check your internet connection.</li>
      <li>Verify that you have authorized the app to access Apple Music in iOS Settings.</li>
      <li>Note: Some DRM-protected tracks, personal custom library songs, or regional restrictions might prevent playback in third-party apps.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>How do I back up my setup?</h3>
    <p>
      Use the backup feature in {site.name} to export your boards, sounds, scripts, rosters,
      and settings. Backups can be stored locally or in iCloud. Pro users also get automatic backups.
    </p>

    <h2>Links</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={url('/')}>Home</a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href={url('/faq')}>FAQ</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose h1 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
